   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi all,<div><br></div><div>Is it possible to use definition variables with lavaan? If not, is this on the roadmap?</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div><br></div><div>Jack</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "z_yxT_pBBgAJ",
   "from": "Terrence Jorgensen",
   "author": "3fe90052fbf2f899",
   "date": "2018-03-27T10:15:04Z",
   "subject": "Re: Definition Variables",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Is it possible to use definition variables with lavaan? If not, is this on the roadmap?</div></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Can you be more specific?  If you are referring to (e.g.) the ability to provide case-specific fixed loadings defined in rows of the data frame, then no, and I doubt it is in any way straight-forward to implement in lavaan because of its use of the parameter table.  You can do this in OpenMx, though.  If you are familiar with Bayesian software, you could also fit a more basic model in blavaan, save the JAGS or Stan syntax (without fitting the model), then update that syntax to use definition variables in place of specific fixed values.</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Postdoctoral Researcher, Methods and Statistics</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">UvA web page: <a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792416812858000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0ITXLmLZq-genHz0kLaQcX\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div><div><br></div></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "7uJ_nv1IBgAJ",
   "from": "Jack Bailey",
   "author": "afad425dd9c86301",
   "date": "2018-03-27T12:23:34Z",
   "subject": "Re: Definition Variables",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Terrence, <div><br></div><div>Case-specific factor loadings was exactly what I was thinking. I ended up fitting the model in OpenMx, but would prefer to do it in lavaan. Doing it &quot;Bayesian-ly&quot; was another possibility that I considered. Thanks, nonetheless.</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>On Tuesday, 27 March 2018 11:15:04 UTC+1, Terrence Jorgensen  wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Is it possible to use definition variables with lavaan? If not, is this on the roadmap?</div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>Can you be more specific?  If you are referring to (e.g.) the ability to provide case-specific fixed loadings defined in rows of the data frame, then no, and I doubt it is in any way straight-forward to implement in lavaan because of its use of the parameter table.  You can do this in OpenMx, though.  If you are familiar with Bayesian software, you could also fit a more basic model in blavaan, save the JAGS or Stan syntax (without fitting the model), then update that syntax to use definition variables in place of specific fixed values.</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Postdoctoral Researcher, Methods and Statistics</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">UvA web page: <a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792416812859000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0quU89ZeVxKlUXWhgQ5k36\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div><div><br></div></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ]
